'''
{'cve_id': 'CVE-2022-1785', 'vulnerability_behavior': {'preconditions_for_vulnerability': 'Lack of proper locking mechanism around text modification and window switching operations during expression evaluation.', 'trigger_condition': 'An attacker crafts a substitute command with an expression that attempts to modify text or switch windows, leading to out-of-bounds writes or other unintended behavior.', 'specific_code_behavior_causing_vulnerability': 'The code does not enforce restrictions on text modifications and window switches during expression evaluations, allowing these operations to occur and potentially leading to out-of-bounds writes.'}, 'solution_behavior': 'To mitigate the vulnerability, it is necessary to add locking mechanisms to block text modifications and window switches during expression evaluations. This ensures that the code operates within a controlled environment and prevents out-of-bounds writes. In this case, the solution involves incrementing a lock variable before evaluating the expression and decrementing it afterward to enforce the restrictions.'}
